{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2123","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Tournament"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array of integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\dots,a_n$$$. A tournament is held with $$$n$$$ players. Player $$$i$$$ has strength $$$a_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"While more than $$$k$$$ players remain, "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Two remaining players are chosen at random; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Then the chosen player with the lower strength is eliminated. If the chosen players have the same strength, one is eliminated at random. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given integers $$$j$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\leq j,k \\leq n$$$), determine if there is any way for player $$$j$$$ to be one of the last $$$k$$$ remaining players."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 10^4$$$)  — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$j$$$, and $$$k$$$ ($$$2\\leq n \\leq 2\\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$1\\leq j, k\\leq n$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers, $$$a_1,a_2,\\dots,a_n$$$ ($$$1\\leq a_i\\leq n$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2\\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output on a single line \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if player $$$j$$$ can be one of the last $$$k$$$ remaining players, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer in any case (upper or lower). For example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be recognized as positive responses."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n5 2 3\n3 2 4 4 1\n5 4 1\n5 3 4 5 2\n6 1 1\n1 2 3 4 5 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nYES\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, suppose that players $$$2$$$ and $$$5$$$ are chosen. Then player $$$2$$$ defeats player $$$5$$$. Now, the remaining player strengths are "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"},{"kind":"text","text":" Next, suppose that players $$$3$$$ and $$$4$$$ are chosen. Then player $$$3$$$ might defeat player $$$4$$$. Now, the remaining player strengths are "},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"4"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"},{"kind":"text","text":" Player $$$2$$$ is one of the last three players remaining."},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third sample, it can be shown that there is no way for player $$$1$$$ to be the last player remaining."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"2123B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2123/problem/B"}